BasisDB
-------

An experimental database in Rust. Pre-release.

The goal is SQLite-like local use, Spanner-style distributed transactions,
and SQL, KV, document, object and analytical interfaces over typed IRs.
Each interface keeps its semantics and lowers to specialized operators
and data layouts. Think MLIR for databases.

Current code includes a pure Raft state machine, a segmented WAL, a
replicated KV service and a Jepsen harness. SQL, MVCC, distributed
transactions and bounded-time integration are not implemented yet.

TrueTime-style guarantees will require a supported bounded-time source.
The first target is AWS ClockBound on supported EC2 hardware.

Build
-----
Requires Rust 1.95+ and protoc.

    git clone https://github.com/windsornguyen/basisdb
    cd basisdb
    cargo build --release --locked
    cargo test --workspace --locked
    ./target/release/bdb start --config basisdb.example.toml

